#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int arr[5];
    int sum = 0;

    // Input five numbers
    cout << "Enter five numbers:\n";
    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        cout << "Number " << i + 1 << ": ";
        cin >> arr[i];
        sum += arr[i];
    }

    // Display in reverse order
    cout << "\nNumbers in reverse order: ";
    for (int i = 4; i >= 0; i--) {
        cout << arr[i] << " ";
    }

    // Calculate and display average
    double average = sum / 5.0;
    cout << "\nAverage: " << average << endl;

    return 0;
}
```

**Program Explanation:**
The program declares an array of size 5 to store integers. A loop inputs five numbers from the user while simultaneously calculating their sum. A second loop displays the array elements in reverse order by iterating from index 4 to 0. Finally, the average is calculated by dividing the sum by 5.0 (using floating-point division) and displayed to the user. The program demonstrates fundamental array operations: input, traversal, and mathematical computation.

